P8 (issue #23, U18): the pattern spectrum row of size 0 may hold
several supports.

resize keeps a single counter for size 0 (the empty set has one support
when item sets are mined), but when a second support arrives it
reallocates the row to one counter and clears the counters beyond it:
a heap buffer overflow (AddressSanitizer in resize, -ge -m0 on data with
empty transactions, where the estimation spreads size 0 over several
supports). The row of size 0 is now sized like every other row; mined
spectra are unchanged.

--- a/tract/src/patspec.c
+++ b/tract/src/patspec.c
@@ -255,7 +255,7 @@
   else if (supp < row->max +BLKSIZE) max = row->max +BLKSIZE;
   else                               max = supp;
   if (max > psp->maxsupp)            max = psp->maxsupp;
-  if (size <= 0) min = max = supp; /* only one counter for size = 0 */
+  /* P8: no single-counter row for size 0 (it overflowed) */
   n = (size_t)max -(size_t)min +1; /* compute the new array size */
   p = (size_t*)realloc(row->frqs, n *sizeof(size_t));
   if (!p) return psp->err = -1; /* enlarge the counter array */
